  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 娘\ntitle: daughter; girl\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-8, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 10\nradical: 女\nradicalNumber: 38\nonyomi: [ジョウ]\nkunyomi: [むすめ, こ]\ndistractors: [始, 銀, 食]\n---\n\n# 娘 — daughter; girl\n\n**Strokes:** 10 · **Key (radical):** 女 (no. 38) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\nLearn 娘 first through [娘](../words/娘.md) (むすめ), \"daughter.\" A person's daughter can be an adult: the family relationship does not disappear with age.\nThe same word also has a young-woman sense, so context matters when no parent is identified.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** picture 女 beside a tall name tag shaped like 良, marking the daughter's place in a family photo.\nThis visual story is not a historical derivation.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| むすめ | kun | [娘](../words/娘.md) (むすめ) — daughter; 一人娘 (ひとりむすめ) — only daughter |\n\nジョウ and こ remain in the source metadata; the table focuses on the reading needed for these words.\n\n## Common words\n\n- [娘](../words/娘.md) (むすめ) — daughter\n- 一人娘 (ひとりむすめ) — only daughter\n\n## Notes\n\nThe right side is 良-shaped, with a top dot. Compare the related lower outlines in [銀](銀.md) and [食](食.md), without treating them as identical components.\n一人娘 says there is only one daughter; it does not by itself say there are no sons.\n\nSources: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project); [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1531190, 1163870.\n",
